# Production Muse runs every hook under one session key (MUSE_SESSION_ID), so
# root and child hooks share one state dir. Payload shapes below mirror
# captured production envelopes: child Start/Stop carry both session ids
# plus a subagent name, child tools carry the child session id only. A
# finished child must release the foreground veto there; otherwise the
# first subagent of a session silences every later bell and freezes the
# busy mark on. Team-mark mapping cannot resolve here — _busy_hook wraps
# each call in a fresh process, so the PPID-keyed owner map never hits —
# which pins child tools as team no-ops, as in production for named
# internal children.
shared_log="$MOCK_BUSY_DIR/muse-shared-child.log"
shared_session="$TEST_SID-muse-shared"
shared_child_a="$TEST_SID-muse-shared-child-a"
shared_child_b="$TEST_SID-muse-shared-child-b"
