# A foreground tool that runs while a child is active must still route as
# root work: with a shared state dir the veto marker alone cannot tell a
# root tool from a child tool, and routing it as a child records the
# session as its own team child — an entry nothing ever removes, so the
# busy mark survives every later Stop. Pre-create the parent mapping that
# _busy_hook's per-call wrappers cannot establish (each hook runs under a
# fresh wrapper pid, so the PPID-keyed owner map never hits even for UUID
# children), so the team path is genuinely exercised; the reminder-shaped
# child id is equivalent downstream of that seam.
